<h1 hidden>Home</h1>

<p>Hey.</p>

<h2>About me</h2>
<p>
    My name is Laura, I go by she/her and I am a software engineer with over 15 
    years of professional experience located in the Netherlands. I am passionate 
    about writing code and I have extensive, in-depth knowledge about C#, .NET 
    and React.
</p>
<aside class="span-many">
    <figure>
        <img class="main-avatar" src="~/images/april-fei.png" width="300" height="425" alt="A Keeper of the Moon Miqo'te from Final Fantasy XIV, wielding a Red Mage's rapier and surrounded by a Black Mage's ice, fire and lightning." />
        <figcaption>April Reaupe by <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:bvzq3tuhdhwq5mkf6jiidwrl">Fei Hsaio</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
</aside>
<p>
    I enjoy programming; it was my hobby before I made it my job. It is for this 
    reason — <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI#Ethical_concerns" rel="external" target="_blank">and many, many others</a> — that I am vehemently 
    <strong>against any and all use of generative AI.</strong> I also don’t shy 
    away from fixing bugs and maintaining and upgrading legacy code, and I have 
    pushed for unit testing, test-driven development, better coding guidelines 
    and code reviews in the past.
</p>
<p>
    In addition to coding, I am also a UX/UI design enthusiast and have some 
    basic practical experience with wireframing, designing and prototyping user 
    interfaces in Figma.
</p>

<h2>Personal</h2>
<p>
    On the internet, I go by <b>Vivelin</b> (<span class="ipa">/ˈvɪvəlɪn/</span>, 
    like <i>Vivian</i>). I am passionate about video games<a href="#steam"><sup>[1]</sup></a><a href="#ffxiv"><sup>[2]</sup></a>,
    music<a href="#lastfm"><sup>[3]</sup></a><a href="#bandcamp"><sup>[4]</sup></a>,
    and I spend a lot of time with my wonderful girlfriend.
</p>
<p>
    I also enjoying reading<a href="#storygraph"><sup>[5]</sup></a>, watching shows<a href="#serializd"><sup>[6]</sup></a> and movies<a href="#letterboxd"><sup>[7]</sup></a>.
</p>
<p>
    One of my past projects is a more casual, accessible version of the
    <a href="https://samus.link/" target="_blank">Super Metroid & A Link to the Past crossover randomizer</a>.
    It combines the <abbr title="Super Nintendo Entertainment System">SNES</abbr>
    games <i>Super Metroid</i> and <i>The Legend of Zelda: A Link to the Past</i>
    into a single game, and shuffles the items between both games.
</p>
<p>
    <a asp-page="/Projects/SMZ3">My version of it</a> makes it more casual and
    approachable. It is a Windows desktop app, which allows for better
    integration and enables features such as a built-in voice-enabled item
    tracker. Several community members have contributed custom sprite work as
    well as some features that were not accepted into the original version.
</p>

